completed_at: "2026-09-13T17:15:20.174Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A pbyu ruling records where assurance lives in the noun grammar and the destination row flips from consolidation to target_noun or keep_as_is; pm history acknowledge (or the shared-verb spelling the ruling picks) is the canonical leaf; history-author-acknowledge remains executable as a hidden permanent alias with identical arguments, results and exit codes; Contracts, shell completions, MCP action parity and docs reflect the relocation and the command-grammar gate passes with no positional-shape or help-token budget growth"
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: low
confidence: medium
resolution: Established history acknowledge as the canonical leaf with its permanent hidden legacy alias and retained assurance through an explicit domain-data exception.
expected_result: "Native and legacy author-disposition paths retain arguments, fingerprints, results, action identities and completion behavior without increasing help ceilings."
actual_result: "Native/legacy source and installed-package previews match; Bash routing and exact Zsh/Fish suites pass; contracts, SDK tuple snapshot and agent documentation reflect the shared canonical path. Full validation: 8819 tests, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
