comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T19:57:58.527Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check: pm-tqel (closed) consolidated history-redact/repair/compact/activity/restore and explicitly left history-author-acknowledge at the root; pm-6apl (closed) delivered the ops namespace without assurance. pm-npr3 covers init/config/schema/profile only. This task is the open owner the census rows for assurance and history-author-acknowledge now name."
  "2026-09-13T16:06:35.066Z","harness:codex","Placement ruling: keep assurance and its declaration/verdict actions as explicit keep_as_is rows under the ops capability family because they manage persistent domain data, with no new noun or help-budget expansion. Relocate history-author-acknowledge to history acknowledge through the shared SDK alias table; retain the stable action identity and all parser options."
  "2026-09-13T16:12:47.342Z","harness:codex","Verification: native history acknowledge and the permanent legacy spelling returned identical source-bound dry-run results through the real source CLI and separate packed npm/Bun consumers. Real Bash completion reaches the plan-fingerprint option through both spellings. Live grammar, flag invocation parity and flag lexicon gates passed; the canonical root count decreased from 27 to 26 with unchanged ceilings."
  "2026-09-13T16:31:53.903Z","harness:codex","Full repository run exposed one stale exact Zsh subcommand-list assertion: 8814 tests passed and one expected the pre-relocation history list. Updated the existing expectation to include acknowledge; no behavior or assertion weakened. Initial run produced no coverage report and is recorded as failed proof. All three linked test runs passed independently (60 discovery, 24 native/legacy history, 26 ownership/grammar tests); the corrected shell suite and full exact coverage are rerunning."
  "2026-09-13T16:33:04.148Z","harness:codex","Canonical grammar ruling for ADR pm-pbyu: retain assurance as keep_as_is because its measurements/assertions/gates/verdicts are durable project domain data, and place author disposition under history acknowledge using the shared acknowledge verb. Root compatibility is permanent and hidden. The gate and generated surfaces confirm no help ceiling was raised; 107 existing completion tests now pass with the canonical Zsh child included."
  "2026-09-13T17:15:19.481Z","harness:codex","Final local validation passed 8819 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage. Repository-wide static quality, linked regressions, typecheck, 57 token-surface budgets, Trivy, ShellCheck, secret scan and documentation links passed. Newly packed npm and Bun consumers passed real extension discovery/invocation, native/legacy author preview, item creation/comments/dependencies and npx/bunx acceptance. Implementation closure is prepared for the combined reviewed PR; this does not claim publication of these candidate changes."
